WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.594
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:09.652
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.952 --> 00:00:18.316
Unit twenty-nine: Passive with Modals and Perfect Tenses. Today you will use the passive with must, can, will, should and the present perfect.

4
00:00:18.616 --> 00:00:21.292
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:25.605
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.648
Must be done.

7
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.648
Must be done means a strong obligation in the passive.

8
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.715
Homework must be done.

9
00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:37.306
Your turn. Say: Must be done.

10
00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.342
Must be done.

11
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:43.050
Can be seen.

12
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.793
Can be seen means a possibility in the passive.

13
00:00:47.383 --> 00:00:48.802
The stars can be seen.

14
00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:52.324
Your turn. Say: Can be seen.

15
00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.295
Can be seen.

16
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.167
Has been built.

17
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:02.077
Has been built means a present perfect passive.

18
00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:04.149
The bridge has been built.

19
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.414
Your turn. Say: Has been built.

20
00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:11.477
Has been built.

21
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:13.380
Have been made.

22
00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:17.347
Have been made means a present perfect passive, plural.

23
00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.392
Mistakes have been made.

24
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:22.717
Your turn. Say: Have been made.

25
00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.788
Have been made.

26
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.748
Will be finished.

27
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.935
Will be finished means a future passive.

28
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.015
It will be finished soon.

29
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:37.350
Your turn. Say: Will be finished.

30
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.526
Will be finished.

31
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:43.238
Should be done.

32
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.679
Should be done means advice in the passive.

33
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:48.877
This should be done today.

34
00:01:49.483 --> 00:01:52.577
Your turn. Say: Should be done.

35
00:01:55.433 --> 00:01:56.458
Should be done.

36
00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:57.997
Agent.

37
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.552
Agent means the person who does the action.

38
00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.685
The agent is the builder.

39
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:06.378
Your turn. Say: Agent.

40
00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:10.049
Agent.

41
00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:11.808
Process.

42
00:02:12.817 --> 00:02:15.014
Process means a series of steps.

43
00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:17.372
A process is described.

44
00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:20.566
Your turn. Say: Process.

45
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.331
Process.

46
00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:28.680
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:32.724
Visal, write a passive sentence about a rule at school.

48
00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:42.683
Homework must be done on time. Modal + be + past participle is the passive with a modal. The doer is not important, the rule is.

49
00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:45.783
How do we form the perfect passive?

50
00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:57.747
Has or have + been + past participle: The new bridge has been built. Mistakes have been made. For the future: The work will be finished by Friday.

51
00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.211
When is it useful?

52
00:03:01.317 --> 00:03:14.490
To describe rules, processes and results without naming the agent: The form should be signed. The temple can be seen from here. Use by only if the agent is important.

53
00:03:15.633 --> 00:03:17.482
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:24.542
Grammar focus: Passive: modal plus be plus past participle; has and have been plus past participle.

55
00:03:24.842 --> 00:03:26.006
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.717 --> 00:03:28.681
Homework must be done on time.

57
00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:30.956
The bridge has been built.

58
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.896
The work will be finished by Friday.

59
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:44.097
Modal + be + past participle. Has / have been + past participle. Will be + past participle. Add by + agent only if it matters.

60
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.605
Be careful! Don't say: Homework must do on time.

61
00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.891
Say: Homework must be done on time.

62
00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:55.249
Use be + past participle.

63
00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.906
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.282
Rules and Processes.

65
00:04:01.582 --> 00:04:04.359
At our school, homework must be done on time.

66
00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:08.318
The library can be used until six o'clock.

67
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:11.995
The new bridge has been built by a local company.

68
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.930
The work will be finished by Friday.

69
00:04:15.933 --> 00:04:18.432
The process should be explained clearly.

70
00:04:19.533 --> 00:04:23.616
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.090
Homework blank on time.

72
00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.124
A, must be done. B, must do. C, must be doing.

73
00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.480
The answer is A: must be done.

74
00:04:36.617 --> 00:04:38.361
The bridge blank last year.

75
00:04:38.661 --> 00:04:42.848
A, has been built. B, is built been. C, was been build.

76
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.934
The answer is A: has been built.

77
00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:52.094
The report blank by Friday.

78
00:04:52.394 --> 00:04:56.385
A, will be finished. B, will finished. C, will be finish.

79
00:04:59.933 --> 00:05:01.979
The answer is A: will be finished.

80
00:05:03.117 --> 00:05:04.466
Which is correct?

81
00:05:04.766 --> 00:05:10.103
A, It can see from here.. B, It can be seen from here.. C, It can be seeing from here..

82
00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:16.374
The answer is B: It can be seen from here..

83
00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:20.677
According to the reading, until when can the library be used?

84
00:05:20.977 --> 00:05:24.700
A, six o'clock. B, noon. C, midnight.

85
00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.638
The answer is A: six o'clock.

86
00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:34.834
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.683 --> 00:05:38.914
Write a sentence with a passive modal about a rule at school.

88
00:05:47.717 --> 00:05:49.182
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:49.482 --> 00:06:00.949
Mobile phones must be switched off during lessons. Homework should be handed in on Monday. These rules are written in the passive because the rule is more important than the person.

90
00:06:01.249 --> 00:06:03.063
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:12.698
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive: modal plus be plus past participle; has and have been plus past participle.

92
00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:16.985
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:17.285 --> 00:06:19.554
See you in Unit thirty. Goodbye!

94
00:06:19.854 --> 00:06:22.541
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

